From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: knapcio <knapcio@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:55:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/30] DFlash2 after prefix reuse and alone on MTP behind
 G6_DFL_REUSE=1|2

A reuse hit that skipped into the drafter's 2,048-row window used to put the request on
MTP for life. Mode 1: the session keeps the drafter. dfl_start fills the rows the prefill
tapped (past the hit); Batch tracks what the drafter's KV ring holds (writer's tokens, lo,
end, top) and, when the last DFlash2 session there had this prompt's tokens up to the hit
and its rows are not wrapped, the context starts at the window's start (turn N+1 after a
DFlash2 turn N). A hit with no prefill at all (a replay) is allowed too. With fewer than
G6_DFL_REUSE_MIN (default 256) context rows the session runs MTP rounds that feed the
drafter until it holds them, then DFlash2. Mode 2: a session alone on MTP (it was not alone
at its prompt tail, or was demoted) takes the drafter the same way. Drafts only; unset =
the previous behaviour. Host test batch_dflreuse_test.
